00:00:12.345 --> 00:00:14.180
VANESSA YURKEVICH, HELLO!
VANESSA WHAT IS CAUSING THE

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:16.182
PRICE SURGE?
&gt;&gt; MANY AMERICANS WOULD GO TO

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:20.487
THE GROCERY STORE, NOT THINK
ANYTHING MUCH ABOUT BUYING A

00:00:20.487 --> 00:00:23.990
DOZEN EGGS NOT REALLY LOOKING AT
PRICES'S CONSIDERED AND IS

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:26.192
CONSIDERED A STAPLE IN AMERICAN
HOUSEHOLDS.

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:29.696
JUST IN THE LAST YEAR A BIG
PRICE INCREASE.

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:32.966
IT STARTED LAST YEAR ABOUT
$1.25.

00:00:32.966 --> 00:00:41.974
UNTO $1.75 NOW ITS $4 H.25 NOW
BECAUSE OF THE DEADLY BIRD FLU

00:00:41.974 --> 00:00:46.579
THAT HAPPENED LAST SPRING AND
IT'S CATCHING UP TO US RIGHT

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:48.881
NOW.
IN ALASKA DEMAND FOR CHICKENS

00:00:48.881 --> 00:00:52.519
AND THEIR EGGS IS HEATING UP.
&gt;&gt; ALREADY SOLD OUT EVEN BEFORE

00:00:52.519 --> 00:00:54.921
THE EGG SHORTAGE.
SELLING EVERYTHING I HAD.

00:00:54.921 --> 00:00:56.990
&gt;&gt; Reporter: IF THE YOU'VE BEEN
TO THE GROCERY STORE RECENTLY

00:00:56.990 --> 00:01:00.360
YOU MAY HAVE NOTICED FEWER EGGS
AND HIGHER PRICES.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:05.064
UP ABOUT 11% LAST MONTH ON
AVERAGE FROM NOVEMBER, UP NEARLY

00:01:05.064 --> 00:01:13.640
60% IN THE LAST YEAR.
$11.49 IN NEW YORK.

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:15.241
$10.99 IN HAWAII.
&gt;&gt; RIDICULOUS.

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:19.612
&gt;&gt; Reporter: THE HIGHLY PATH
GENIC AVIAN INFLUENZA OR AVIAN

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:23.816
FLU IS LARGELY TO BLAME.
NEARLY 58 MILLION BIRDS AND

00:01:23.816 --> 00:01:27.220
CLIMBING HAVE DIED ACROSS 47
STATES IN THE LAST YEAR.

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:31.925
A RESULT OF THE DEADLY VIRUS.
WILD BIRDS CAN CARRY THE DISEASE

00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:35.762
AND SPREAD IT TO DOMESTIC FLOCKS
WHEN THEY MIGRATE.

00:01:35.762 --> 00:01:39.532
&gt;&gt; ONE WILD BIRD COMING INTO
THEIR CHICKEN RUN AND THE NEXT

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:45.438
THING YOU KNOW, 10 BIRDS, 20
BIRDS, 30 BIRDS JUST DROPPING

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:47.340
DEAD.
&gt;&gt; Reporter: SOME STATES

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:51.244
RECOMMENDING ALL POULTRY BE
MAINTAINED INDOORS.

00:01:51.244 --> 00:01:58.017
POULTRY AND BIRD SHOWS CANCELED,
STRICTLY ENFORCED.

00:01:58.017 --> 00:02:00.653
&gt;&gt; THE AVIAN BIRD FLU IS
SERIOUS.

00:02:00.653 --> 00:02:06.292
&gt;&gt; Reporter: STRUGGLING WITH
PRICES ON THEIR MAIN INGREDIENT.

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:14.334
THE FALL MIGRATION OF FALL BIRDS
SENT AVIAN FLU CASES SPIKING

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:15.768
AGAIN.
&gt;&gt; WE GO THROUGH A SIGNIFICANT

00:02:15.768 --> 00:02:18.738
AMOUNT OF EGGS.
THE LAST COUPLE OF EGGS JUMPED

00:02:18.738 --> 00:02:21.708
AS HIGH AS 60%.
&gt;&gt; Reporter: HOW HAVE YOU BEEN

00:02:21.708 --> 00:02:25.645
ABLE TO ABSORB THE HIGH PRICES
OF EGGS?

00:02:25.645 --> 00:02:30.883
&gt;&gt; UNFORTUNATELY RAISED ALL
PRICES 10%.

00:02:30.883 --> 00:02:33.720
&gt;&gt; Reporter: FOR SOME INCREASE
IS TOO MUCH.

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:36.256
A BREAKRY IN NEBRASKA CLOSES ITS
DOORS THIS WEEKEND.

00:02:36.256 --> 00:02:39.659
&gt;&gt; I THINK ABOUT WHAT OUR FAMILY
COULD AFFORD TO PAY FOR A

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:41.928
COOKIE.
I TAKE THAT INTO CONSIDERATION.

00:02:41.928 --> 00:02:46.065
WE CAN'T CHARGE $5 A COOKIE.
&gt;&gt; Reporter: THE RIPPLE EFFECT

00:02:46.065 --> 00:02:47.867
GOES BEYOND RESTAURANTS AND
BAKERIES.

00:02:47.867 --> 00:02:50.536
TAKE A LOOK AROUND THE GROCERY
STORE.

00:02:50.536 --> 00:02:55.475
ITEMS THAT USE EGGS LIKE
MAYONNAISE, UP 1.8% IN THE LAST

00:02:55.475 --> 00:03:00.980
YEAR.
&gt;&gt; FROM THE FLU TO THE INCREASES

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:05.084
IN INFLATION, ALL COMBINED
TOGETHER WITH THE SHORTAGE,

00:03:05.084 --> 00:03:06.853
PERFECT STORM.
&gt;&gt; DEFINITELY SEEING PRICES

00:03:06.853 --> 00:03:09.389
SHOOT UP RECENTLY.
&gt;&gt; Reporter: DOES THE THAT STOP

00:03:09.389 --> 00:03:11.791
YOU FROM MAKING THE PURCHASE?
&gt;&gt; NO.

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:15.194
NOT AT ALL.
JUST BUYING THINGS TO MAKE A

00:03:15.194 --> 00:03:18.331
CHICKEN CUTLET AND EGGS IS THE
BASIS FOR THAT TOO.

00:03:18.331 --> 00:03:21.801
ONE OF THE WAYS THERE'S JUST NO
WAY NOT TO PURCHASE THEM.

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:24.470
&gt;&gt; Reporter: GOOD NEWS FROM THE
U.S. DEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE.

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:28.174
THIS WEEK THEY SAID PRICES ARE
STARTING TO FALL A LITTLE BIT,

00:03:28.174 --> 00:03:32.812
BUT THAT SUPPLY REMAINS LIGHT TO
MODERATE, AND, YOU KNOW,

00:03:32.812 --> 00:03:35.348
